   <indicator measure="5">
    <title>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">Status of Implementation Progress: Total 5,345 km of additional pipeline laid in project districts (North 24 Pargana, East Medinipur and Bankura. For (i) North 24 Pargana: Households survey completed, capturing data for 93,240 households; (ii) Bankura: Completed, capturing data for 1,21,000 HHs; and (iii) East Medinipur: Households survey completed. For (i) North 24 Parganas: Construction of 100 MLD WTP in progress; (ii) Bankura: Construction of 44 MLD and 36 MLD WTP in progress; and (iii) East Medinipur - Construction of 112 MLD WTP in progress. For (i) North 24 Parganas: Construction in progress at 30 Storage reservoir sites; (ii) Bankura: Construction in progress at 54 Storage reservoir sites; and (iii) East Medinipur: Construction in progress at 15 Storage reservoir sites. For (i) North 24 Parganas: Construction is in progress for water treatment plan and work completed at 16 out 39 OHRs; and (ii) Bankura: work is in progress for storage reservoirs. District-wise DWQAP report submitted by PMC. Water Safety Plan for districts of North 24 Pargana and Bankura developed and approved. Fecal sludge and septage management expert engaged and mobilized. Draft report has been prepared by the expert. Implementation of awareness campaigns are being undertaken in all 3 districts. More than 40% female participation reported in awareness campaigns conducted so far. Flood forecasting and early warning system modelling with secondary data completed. Training module preparation is ongoing. Poverty mapping and identification of female and male candidates for skill training were substantially completed. Resolution from all 66 GPs for implementation of AMSDF has been obtained and process for ensuring adoption by the project team panchayats is under progress. Smart water management application has been rolled out in three sample GPs. Gender strategy for PHED is being under preparation.</narrative>
    </title>
